[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Bird Flight]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:01.00]Lesson 23 | 第23课
[00:02.98]Bird flight | 鸟的飞行
[00:10.52]What are the two main types of bird flight described by the author? | 作者描述了哪两种主要的鸟类飞行方式？
[00:17.99]No two sorts of birds practise quite the same sort of flight; | 没有两种鸟的飞行方式是完全相同的，
[00:23.47]the varieties are infinite; but two classes may be roughly seen. | 其种类千变万化；但大致可分为两类。
[00:29.45]Any ship that crosses the Pacific | 任何横渡太平洋的轮船，
[00:31.59]is accompanied for many days by the smaller albatross, | 都会有较小的信天翁一连多天伴随着，
[00:36.85]which may keep company with the vessel for an hour | 信天翁可能随船飞行一小时，
[00:40.10]without visible or more than occasional movement of wing. | 却看不见翅膀扇动，或至多偶尔动一动。
[00:45.71]The currents of air that the walls of the ship direct upwards, | 船体两侧导向上升的气流，
[00:50.11]as well as in the line of its course, | 以及沿其航线的气流，
[00:53.78]are enough to give the great bird with its immense wings | 足以使这种长着巨大翅膀的大鸟
[00:57.45]sufficient sustenance and progress. | 得到足够的支撑和前进的动力。
[01:00.84]The albatross is the king of the gliders, | 信天翁是滑翔飞行之王，
[01:04.30]the class of fliers which harness the air to their purpose, | 是那一类驾驭空气为自身目的服务的飞鸟，
[01:08.22]but must yield to its opposition. | 但必须向空气的阻力屈服。
[01:11.61]In the contrary school, the duck is supreme. | 在与此相反的一派中，鸭子是无与伦比的。
[01:16.22]It comes nearer to the engines with which man has 'conquered' the air, as he boasts. | 它们更接近于人类引以自豪地用来“征服”了天空的发动机。
[01:22.79]Duck, and like them the pigeons, are endowed with steel-like muscles, | 鸭子，和与它们相似的鸽子，都长着钢一般的肌肉，
[01:30.24]that are a good part of the weight of the bird, | 这肌肉占去了鸟体重量的很大一部分，
[01:33.32]and these will ply the short wings with such irresistible power | 它们以不可抗拒的力量挥动短翅膀，
[01:38.48]that they can bore for long distances through an opposing gale | 使它们能在顶风的情况下穿行很远的距离
[01:43.04]before exhaustion follows. | 才感到疲劳。
[01:45.74]Their humbler followers, such as partridges, | 它们较为卑微的追随者，比如鹧鸪，
[01:49.64]have a like power of strong propulsion, but soon tire. | 也有同样强的推进力，但很快就疲劳了。
[01:54.30]You may pick them up in utter exhaustion, | 如果海上刮来的风迫使它们作长途飞行，
[01:57.52]if wind over the sea has driven them to a long journey. | 你可以在它们精疲力竭时把它们拾起来。
[02:01.78]The swallow shares the virtues of both schools in highest measure. | 燕子最大限度地兼有两派的优点。
[02:06.53]It tires not, nor does it boast of its power; but belongs to the air | 它不知疲倦，也不夸耀自己的力量；它属于天空，
[02:13.01]travelling it may be six thousand miles to and from its northern nesting home, | 往返于北方的筑巢地，行程可达6000英里，
[02:18.95]feeding its flown young as it flies, and slipping through a medium | 一边飞一边喂养出飞的雏鸟，轻盈地穿过一种
[02:23.37]that seems to help its passage even when the wind is adverse. | 即使在逆风时似乎也有助于它飞行的介质。
[02:28.78]Such birds do us good, | 这样的鸟对我们有益，
[02:30.91]though we no longer take omens from their flight on this side and that; | 尽管我们不再从它们的飞行中占卜吉凶；
[02:36.29]and even the most superstitious villagers no longer take off their hats to the magpie and wish it good-morning. | 就连最迷信的村民也不再向喜鹊脱帽致意、道声早安了。
